---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Why Blox held an order instead of cancelling it';
const description =
	'Blox holds an order for review when it has already cancelled several orders for the same customer recently.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} noindex>
	<article class="doc section">
		<div class="site-wrap doc__wrap">
			<span class="section-label">Docs</span>
			<h1>{title}</h1>
			<div class="doc__body">
				<p>
					Blox had already cancelled several orders for this customer in a short time. That’s
					unusual, so it held this order for you to review rather than cancelling and refunding
					another one.
				</p>
				<p>
					A run of cancellations sometimes means more than one shopper has ended up under a single
					customer profile. Cancelling can’t be undone. A hold can, so the decision is left to you.
				</p>
				<p>Either way the order is stopped, and nothing ships until you decide.</p>

				<h2>What to do</h2>
				<p>
					Open the customer from the link in your notification and review the orders under that
					profile.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>One person, correctly blocked</strong> — cancel the held order.</li>
					<li>
						<strong>More than one shopper grouped together</strong> — release the hold and let us
						know at <a href="mailto:hello@heyblox.com">hello@heyblox.com</a>.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Blox resumes cancelling on its own once those earlier cancellations are more than 24 hours
					old.
				</p>
				<p>
					Questions, or a profile that has grouped the wrong people? Email{' '}
					<a href="mailto:hello@heyblox.com">hello@heyblox.com</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.doc {
		padding-top: 3.5rem;
		padding-bottom: 5rem;
	}

	.doc__wrap {
		max-width: 46rem;
	}

	.doc h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
		margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
	}

	.doc__body h2 {
		margin: 2.5rem 0 0.85rem;
		font-size: 1.35rem;
	}

	.doc__body p {
		margin: 0.85rem 0;
		color: var(--color-fg-muted);
	}

	.doc__body ul {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		color: var(--color-fg-muted);
	}

	.doc__body li {
		margin: 0.4rem 0;
	}

	.doc__body a {
		color: var(--color-fg);
	}

	.doc__body strong {
		color: var(--color-fg);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
</style>
